Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: restore CX GBIF configuration for A640 and A680

The CX GBIF setup was moved from hw_init() to a6xx_gmu_fw_start(),
using the gbif_cx register list in the GPU catalog.  The former code
covered adreno_is_a640_family(), but neither GEN2 entry (A640/A680)
has a gbif_cx list.  Both now skip programming GBIF_QSB_SIDE0..3.

Attach the existing a640_gbif list to both entries to restore the four
0x00071620 writes through the new initialization path.  Other families
and the GX client QoS configuration are unchanged.

This fixes an initialization omission visible in the 7.2.6 source.
Whether it also fixes the nabu CCU translation faults needs hardware
A/B testing; no Tested-by or claim of a confirmed fault fix is made.

Link: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2025/11/12/663
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -983,6 +983,7 @@
 		.a6xx = &(const struct a6xx_info) {
 			.hwcg = a640_hwcg,
 			.protect = &a630_protect,
+			.gbif_cx = a640_gbif,
 			.gmu_cgc_mode = 0x00020202,
 			.prim_fifo_threshold = 0x00180000,
 		},
@@ -1106,6 +1107,7 @@
 		.a6xx = &(const struct a6xx_info) {
 			.hwcg = a640_hwcg,
 			.protect = &a630_protect,
+			.gbif_cx = a640_gbif,
 			.gmu_cgc_mode = 0x00020202,
 			.prim_fifo_threshold = 0x00200200,
 		},
